UID:3343-1792832400-1792839600@www.bloorwestvillagebia.com
SUMMARY:Guided Fall Colours Walking Tour: Bloor West Village to High Park
DESCRIPTION:🍁 Join local nature photographer Richard Bod for a walking tour through one of the city’s most spectacular spots for fall colours: High Park. Richard will guide you through some of the park’s history\, fascinating stories\, wildlife\, and hidden corners as you take in the sights and sounds of the season. \nMake a day of it—grab lunch\, browse local shops and explore Bloor West Village before or after your walk. Daytrip ideas \n🗓️ Sat\, Oct 24 | 9–11 AM\n📍 Meeting Location: Neil McLellan Park\, 263 Beresford Ave (Northwest entrance)\n🔗 Only 25 spots available. \nRegister Here!\nWhat To Expect\n🔹 A guided walk starting at Neil McLellan Park into the northwest corner of High Park\, along Grenadier Pond\n🔹 Beautiful autumn foliage and seasonal landscapes\n🔹 Stories about High Park’s history and natural environment\n🔹 Plenty of opportunities for photographs \n🔹 This walk begins and ends in Bloor West Village! Enjoy all the village offers \nAbout the Speaker\nRichard Bod is a local nature photographer who has spent years working with organizations like the High Park Nature Centre\, Toronto Wildlife Centre\, and the Owl Foundation. Visit his work at richardbodphotography.ca \nCover photo shot by Richard Bod
URL:https://www.bloorwestvillagebia.com/event/guided-fall-colours-walking-tour-bloor-west-village-to-high-park/
LOCATION:Neil McLellan Park\, 263 Beresford Ave\, Toronto\, ON\, M6S 2Y6\, Canada
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.bloorwestvillagebia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Bloor-West-Village-Walking-tour.png
ORGANIZER;CN="Bloor West Village BIA":MAILTO:info@bloorwestvillagebia.com
END:VEVENT
